{
  "title": "Other Aamal of the First Night",
  "data": "Acts of the Night\nHusband and wife are recommended to have intercourse tonight; it is otherwise disliked on the first night of a lunar month.\nPerform ghusl tonight.\nBathe in a flowing river, pouring thirty handfuls of water over the head.\nVisit the tomb of Imam al-Husayn (a.s.).\nBegin the [One Thousand Unit Prayers](AA4) of Ramazan tonight.\nPray two units, reciting in each [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) and [Surah al-An'am](A10), then ask Allah for security against apprehensions and ailments.\nRecite [Dua Jawshan Kabir](E29).\nRecite [Dua Hajj](AA9).",
  "tabs": [
    "Allahumma Inna Hadha al-Shahr al-Mubarak\nاَللَّهُمَّ اِنَّ هٰذَا الشَّهْرَ الْمُبَارَكَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNA HAADHASH SHAHRAL MUBAARAK\nO Allah, this blessed month\nالَّذِي اُنْزِلَ فِيْهِ الْقُرْاٰنُ\nALLADHEE UNZILA FEEHIL QUR'AAN\nin which the Qur'an was revealed\nوَجُعِلَ هُدَىً لِلنَّاسِ\nWA JU'ILA HUDAA LIN NAAS\nand was made guidance for people\nوَبَيِّنَاتٍ مِنَ الْهُدَىٰ وَالْفُرْقَانِ\nWA BAYYINAATIN MINAL HUDAA WAL FURQAAN\nand clear proofs of the guidance, and the Criterion (of right and wrong),\nقَدْ حَضَرَ\nQAD HADAR\nhas commenced.\nفَسَلِّمْنَا فِيْهِ\nFASALLIMNAA FEEH\nSo, (please) keep us out of blemish during it,\nوَسَلَّمْهُ لَنَا\nWA SALLAMHU LANAA\nkeep it sound for us,\nوَتَسَلَّمْهُ مِنَّا فِيْ يُسْرٍ مِنْكَ وَعَافِيَةٍ\nWA TASALLAMHU MINNAA FEE YUSRIN MINKA WA A'AFIYAH\nand receive it from us with means of easiness and good health from You.\nيَا مَنْ اَخَذَ الْقَلِيلَ وَشَكَرَ الْكَثِيرَ\nYAA MAN AKHADHAL QALEELA WA SHAKARAL KATHEER\nO He Who has accepted the little (deed) and thanked for the much,\nاقْبَلْ مِنِّي الْيَسِيرَ\nIQBAL MINNIL YASEER\n(please) accept from me the little (deed).\nاَللَّهُمَّ اِنِّي اَسْاَلُكَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS'ALUK\nO Allah, I beseech You\nاَنْ تَجْعَلَ لِي اِلَىٰ كُلِّ خَيْرٍ سَبِيلاً\nAN TAJ'ALA LEE ILAA KULLI KHAYRIN SABEELAA\nto make for me a path to every decency,\nوَمِنْ كُلِّ مَا لَا تُحِبُّ مَانِعاً\nWA MIN KULLI MAA LAA TUHIBBU MAANI'AA\nand to make for me a barrier against everything that You do not like.\nيَا اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِينَ\nYAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEEN\nO most Merciful of all those who show mercy!\nيَا مَنْ عَفَا عَنِّي وَعَمَّا خَلَوْتُ بِهٖ مِنَ السَّيِّئَاتِ\nYAA MAN A'FAA A'NNEE WA A'MMAA KHALAWTU BIHEE MINAS SAYYI'AAT\nO He Who has pardoned me and overlooked the misdeeds that I have committed secretly!\nيَا مَنْ لَمْ يُؤَاخِذْنِي بِارْتِكَابِ الْمَعَاصِي\nYAA MAN LAM YU'AAKHIDHNEE BIRTIKAABIL MA'AASEE\nO He Who has not punished me for my committing acts of disobedience to Him!\nعَفْوَكَ عَفْوَكَ عَفْوَكَ يَا كَرِيمُ\nA'FWAKA A'FWAKA A'FWAKA YAA KAREEM\nI seek Your pardon, I seek Your pardon, I seek Your pardon, O All-generous!\nاِلٰهِي وَعَظْتَنِي فَلَمْ اَتَّعِظْ\nILAAHEE WA A'ZTANEE FALAM ATTA'IZ\nO my God, You advised me, but I have not followed Your advice\nوَزَجَرْتَنِي عَنْ مَحَارِمِكَ فَلَمْ اَنْزَجِرْ\nWA ZAJARTANEE A'N MAHAARIMIKA FALAM ANZAJIR\nand You rebuked me for violating that which You have deemed forbidden, but I have not stopped.\nفَمَا عُذْرِي\nFAMAA U'DHREE\nNow, what is my excuse?\nفَاعْفُ عَنِّي يَا كَرِيمُ\nFA'FU A'NNEE YAA KAREEM\nSo, (please) pardon me, O All-generous!\nعَفْوَكَ عَفْوَكَ\nA'FWAKA A'FWAK\nI seek Your pardon, I seek Your pardon!\nاَللَّهُمَّ اِنِّي اَسْاَلُكَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS'ALUK\nO Allah, I beseech You\nالرَّاحَةَ عِنْدَ الْمَوْتِ\nAR-RAAHATA I'NDAL MAWT\nfor rest at death\nوَالْعَفْوَ عِنْدَ الْحِسَابِ\nWAL A'FWA I'NDAL HISAAB\nand for pardon at calling to account.\nعَظُمَ الذَّنْبُ مِنْ عَبْدِكَ\nA'ZUMADH DHANBU MIN A'BDIK\nGreat is the sin of Your servant;\nفَلْيَحْسُنِ التَّجَاوُزُ مِنْ عِنْدِكَ\nFALYAHSUNIT TAJAAWUZU MIN I'NDIK\nso, let Your overlooking him be excellent.\nيَا اَهْلَ التَّقْوَىٰ وَيَا اَهْلَ الْمَغْفِرَةِ\nYAA AHLAT TAQWAA WA YAA AHLAL MAGHFIRAH\nO He Who is worth being feared and is worth forgiving!\nعَفْوَكَ عَفْوَكَ\nA'FWAKA A'FWAK\nI seek Your pardon, I seek Your pardon.\nاَللَّهُمَّ اِنِّي عَبْدُكَ ابْنُ عَبْدِكَ ابْنُ اَمَتِكَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE A'BDUKABNU A'BDIKABNU AMATIK\nO Allah, I am Your servant and the son of Your servant and Your she-servant\nضَعِيفٌ فَقِيرٌ اِلَىٰ رَحْمَتِكَ\nDA'EEFUN FAQEERUN ILAA RAHMATIK\nand I am weak and in need for Your mercy;\nوَاَنْتَ مُنْزِلُ الْغِنَىٰ وَالْبَرَكَةِ عَلَىٰ الْعِبَادِ\nWA ANTA MUNZILUL GHINAA WAL BARAKATI A'LAL I'BAAD\nwhile You are the Pourer of wealth and bless on the servants (of You),\nقَاهِرٌ مُقْتَدِرٌ\nQAAHIRUN MUQTADIR\nYou are omnipotent and full of power,\nاَحْصَيْتَ اَعْمَالَهُمْ\nAHSAYTA A'MAALAHUM\nYou have recorded all their (i.e. Your servants) deeds,\nوَقَسَمْتَ اَرْزَاقَهُمْ\nWA QASAMTA ARZAAQAHUM\ndecided the sustenance of each one them,\nوَجَعَلْتَهُمْ مُخْتَلِفَةً اَلْسِنَتُهُمْ وَاَلْوَانُهُمْ\nWA JA'ALTAHUM MUKHTALIFATAN ALSINATUHUM WA ALWAANUHUM\nand made them of different languages and colors\nخَلْقاً مِنْ بَعْدِ خَلْقٍ\nKHALQAN MIN BA'DI KHALQ\nin different stages of creation.\nوَلَا يَعْلَمُ الْعِبَادُ عِلْمَكَ\nWA LAA YA'LAMUL I'BAADU I'LMAK\nYour servants can never attain Your knowledge\nوَلَا يَقْدِرُ الْعِبَادُ قَدْرَكَ\nWA LAA YAQDIRUL I'BAADU QADRAK\nand Your servants can never recognize the real estimate that is due to You.\nوَكُلُّنَا فَقِيرٌ اِلَىٰ رَحْمَتِكَ\nWA KULLUNAA FAQEERUN ILAA RAHMATIK\nAll of us are needy for Your mercy.\nفَلَا تَصْرِفْ عَنِّي وَجْهَكَ\nFALAA TASRIF A'NNEE WAJHAK\nSo, (please) do not turn Your Face away from me\nوَاجْعَلْنِيْ مِنْ صَالِحِي خَلْقِكَ\nWAJ'ALNEE MIN SAALIHEE KHALQIK\nand include me with the virtuous creatures of You\nفِيْ الْعَمَلِ وَالْاَمَلِ\nFIL A'MALI WAL AMAL\nin deeds, hopes,\nوَالْقَضَاءِ وَالْقَدَرِ\nWAL QADAA'I WAL QADAR\nand Your decisions (for me).\nاَللَّهُمَّ اَبْقِنِي خَيْرَ الْبَقَاءِ\nALLAAHUMMA ABQINEE KHAYRAL BAQAA'\nO Allah, (please) keep me alive in the best manner of living,\nوَاَفْنِنِي خَيْرَ الْفَنَاءِ عَلَىٰ مُوَالاةِ اَوْلِيَائِكَ\nWA AFNINEE KHAYRAL FANAA'I A'LAA MUWAALAATI AWLIYAA'IK\ndecide for me to die in the best manner of death keeping loyal to Your representatives,\nوَمُعَادَاةِ اَعْدَائِكَ\nWA MU'AADAATI A'DAA'IK\nincurring the enmity of Your enemies,\nوَالرَّغْبَةِ اِلَيْكَ وَالرَّهْبَةِ مِنْكَ\nWAR RAGHBATI ILAYKA WAR RAHBATI MINK\nkeeping desiring for You, fearing from You,\nوَالْخُشُوعِ وَالْوَفَاءِ وَالتَّسْلِيمِ لَكَ\nWAL KHUSHOO'I WAL WAFAA'I WAT TASLEEMI LAK\nand submitting to You, being loyal to You, complying with You,\nوَالتَّصْدِيقِ بِكِتَابِكَ\nWAT TASDEEQI BIKITAABIK\nbelieving in Your Book,\nوَاتِّبَاعِ سُنَّةِ رَسُولِكَ\nWATTIBAA'I SUNNATI RASOOLIK\nand following Your Prophet’s instructions.\nاَللَّهُمَّ مَا كَانَ فِي قَلْبِي\nALLAAHUMMA MAA KAANA FEE QALBEE\nO Allah, as for whatever I bear in my heart,\nمِنْ شَكٍّ اَوْ رِيبَةٍ\nMIN SHAKKIN AW REEBAH\nincluding suspicion, doubt,\nاَوْ جُحُودٍ اَوْ قُنُوطٍ\nAW JUHOODIN AW QUNOOT\ndenial, despair,\nاَوْ فَرَحٍ اَوْ بَذَخٍ اَوْ بَطَرٍ\nAW FARAHIN AW BADHAKHIN AW BATAR\n(excessive) joy, lavish expenditure or recklessness,\nاَوْ خُيَلاءَ اَوْ رِيَاءٍ اَوْ سُمْعَةٍ\nAW KHUYALAA'A AW RIYAA'IN AW SUM'AH\npride, arrogance, ostentation,\nاَوْ شِقَاقٍ اَوْ نِفَاقٍ\nAW SHIQAAQIN AW NIFAAQ\ndiscord, hypocrisy,\nاَوْ كُفْرٍ اَوْ فُسُوقٍ اَوْ عِصْيَانٍ\nAW KUFRIN AW FUSOOQIN AW I'SYAAN\nunbelief, licentiousness, disobedience,\nاَوْ عَظَمَةٍ اَوْ شَيْءٍ لَا تُحِبُّ\nAW A'ZAMATIN AW SHAY'IN LAA TUHIBB\nconceit, or anything else that You do not like;\nفَاَسْاَلُكَ يَا رَبِّ اَنْ تُبَدِّلَنِي مَكَانَهٗ اِيمَاناً بِوَعْدِكَ\nFA-AS'ALUKA YAA RABBI AN TUBADDILANEE MAKAANAHOO EEMAANAN BIWA'DIK\nI thus beseech You, O my Lord, to substitute all that with belief in Your promise,\nوَوَفَاءً بِعَهْدِكَ\nWA WAFAA'AN BI-A'HDIK\nfulfillment of my covenant to You,\nوَرِضاً بِقَضَائِكَ\nWA RIDAN BIQADAA'IK\nsatisfaction with what You decide for me,\nوَزُهْداً فِي الدُّنْيَا\nWA ZUHDAN FID DUNYAA\nindifference to the worldly pleasures,\nوَرَغْبَةً فِيمَا عِنْدَكَ\nWA RAGHBATAN FEEMAA I'NDAK\ndesire for that which You have,\nوَاَثَرَةً وَطُمَاْنِينَةً\nWA ATHARATAN WA TUMA'NEENAH\naltruism, tranquility,\nوَتَوْبَةً نَصُوحاً\nWA TAWBATAN NASOOHAA\nand sincere repentance.\nاَسْاَلُكَ ذٰلِكَ يَا رَبَّ الْعَالَمِينَ\nAS'ALUKA DHAALIKA YAA RABBAL A'ALAMEEN\nI beseech You for all that, O Lord of the worlds!\nاِلٰهِي اَنْتَ مِنْ حِلْمِكَ تُعْصَىٰ فَكَاَنَّكَ لَمْ تُرَ\nILAAHEE ANTA MIN HILMIKA TU'SAA FAKA'ANNAKA LAM TUR\nO my God, because You are so forbearing, You are disobeyed as if You are not present,\nوَمِنْ كَرَمِكَ وَجُودِكَ تُطَاعُ فَكَاَنَّكَ لَمْ تُعْصَ\nWA MIN KARAMIKA WA JOODIKA TUTAA'U FAKA'ANNAKA LAM TU'S\nand because You are so generous and magnanimous, You are obeyed as if You have not been disobeyed at all.\nوَاَنَا وَمَنْ لَمْ يَعْصِكَ سُكَّانُ اَرْضِكَ\nWA ANAA WA MAN LAM YA'SIKA SUKKAANU ARDIK\nBoth those who have not disobeyed You and I are the inhabitants of Your lands;\nفَكُنْ عَلَيْنَا بِالْفَضْلِ جَوَاداً\nFAKUN A'LAYNAA BIL FADLI JAWAADAA\nso, (please) confer magnanimously upon us with Your favors\nوَبِالْخَيْرِ عَوَّاداً\nWA BIL KHAYRI A'WWAADAA\nand always refer to us with Your goodness.\nيَا اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِينَ\nYAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEEN\nO most Merciful of all those who show mercy!\nوَصَلَّىٰ اللَّهُ عَلَىٰ مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِهِ صَلاةً دَائِمَةً\nWA SALLALLAAHU A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIHEE SALAATAN DAA'IMAH\nMay Allah bless Muhammad and his Household with endless blessings\nلَا تُحْصَىٰ وَلَا تُعَدُّ\nLAA TUHSAA WA LAA TU'ADD\nthat are innumerable, uncountable,\nوَلَا يَقْدِرُ قَدْرَهَا غَيْرُكَ\nWA LAA YAQDIRU QADRAHAA GHAYRUK\nand none can do it save You.\nيَا اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِينَ\nYAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEEN\nO most Merciful of all those who show mercy!",
    "Dua Ya Man Yamliku al-Tadbir\nAfter the Maghrib prayer, raise your hands and recite:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ يَا مَنْ يَمْلِكُ التَّدْبِيْرَ وَهُوَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ\nALLAAHUMMA YAA MAN YAMLIKUT TADBEERA WA HUWA A'LAA KULLI SHAY'IN QADEER\nO Allah Who controls the management of all affairs and He has power over all things!\nيَا مَنْ يَعْلَمُ خَآئِنَةَ الْاَعْيُنِ وَمَا تُخْفِيْ الصُّدُوْرِ وَتُجِنُّ الضَّمِيْرُ وَهُوَ اللَّطِيْفُ الْخَبِيْرُ\nYAA MAN YA'LAMU KHAA'INATAL A'YUNI WA MAA TUKHFIS SUDOORI WA TUJINNUD DAMEERU WA HUWAL LATEEFUL KHABEER\nO He Who knows the stealth of looks, that which breasts conceal, and that which selves hide and He is the Knower of subtle, the Aware!\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اجْعَلْنَا مِمَّنْ نَوٰى فَعَمِلَ، وَلَا تَجْعَلْنَا مِمَّنْ شَقِيَ فَكَسِلَ، وَلَا مِمَّنْ هُوَ عَلٰى غَيْرِ عَمَلٍ يَتَّكِلُ\nALLAAHUMMAJ A'LNAA MIMMAN NAWAA FA'AMILA WA LAA TAJ'ALNAA MIMMAN SHAQIYA FAKASILA WA LAA MIMMAN HUWA A'LAA GHAYRI A'MALIN YATTAKIL\nO Allah, (please do) include us with those who intend and carried out their intentions, and do not include us with those who are unhappy due to their laziness or with those who depend upon unreal hopes.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَحِّحْ اَبْدَانَنَا مِنَ الْعِلَلِ، وَاَعِنَّا عَلٰى مَا افْتَرَضْتَ عَلَيْنَا مِنَ الْعَمَلِ، حَتّٰى يَنْقَضِيَ عَنَّا شَهْرُكَ هَذَا وَقَدْ اَدَّيْنَا مَفْرُوْضَكَ فِيْهِ عَلَيْنَا\nALLAAHUMMA SAHHIH ABDAANANAA MINAL I'LALI WA A'INNAA A'LAA MAF TARADTA A'LAYNAA MINAL A'MALI HATTAA YANQADIYA A'NNAA SHAHRUKA HAADHAA WA QAD ADDAYNAA MAFROODAKA FEEHI A'LAYNAA\nO Allah, (please do) cure our bodies from ailments and help us carry out the deeds You have made incumbent upon us to do so that when this month, which is Your month, elapses, we shall have carried out all the duties that You have made obligatory upon us to do.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اَعِنَّا عَلٰى صِيَامِهٖ، وَوَفِّقْنَا لِقِيَامِهٖ، وَنَشِّطْنَا فِيْهِ لِلصَّلَاةِ، وَلَا تَحْجُبْنَا مِنَ الْقِرَاۤءَةِ، وَسَهِّلْ لَنَا فِيْهِ اِيْتَاۤءَ الزَّكَاةِ\nALLAAHUMMA A'INNAA A'LAA SIYAAMIHEE WA WAFFIQNAA LIQIYAAMIHEE WA NASHSHITNAA FEEHI LIS SALAATI WA LAA TAHJUBNAA MINAL QIRAA'ATI WA SAHHIL LANAA FEEHI EETAA'AZ ZAKAAH\nO Allah, (please do) help us observe fasting in this month, guide us to practice the acts of worship (perfectly), grant us vigor to offer prayers, do not preclude us from reciting (the Holy Qur'an), and make easy for us to give alms.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ لَا تُسَلِّطْ عَلَيْنَا وَصَبًا وَلَا تَعَبًا وَلَا سَقَمًا وَلَا عَطَبًا\nALLAAHUMMA LAA TUSALLIT A'LAYNAA WASABAN WA LAA TA'ABAN WA LAA SAQAMAN WA LAA A'TABAA\nO Allah, (please) do not inflict us with fatigue, tiredness, ailment, or injury.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ ارْزُقْنَا الْاِفْطَارَ مِنْ رِزْقِكَ الْحَلَالِ\nALLAAHUMMAR ZUQNAL IFTAARA MIN RIZQIKAL HALAAL\nO Allah, (please do) grant us the food with which we break our fasting from Your sustenance that is legally gotten.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ سَهِّلْ لَنَا فِيْهِ مَا قَسَمْتَهٗ مِنْ رِزْقِكَ، وَيَسِّرْ مَا قَدَّرْتَهٗ مِنْ اَمْرِكَ، وَاجْعَلْهُ حَلَالًا طَيِّبًا نَقِيًّا مِنَ الْاٰثَامِ خَالِصًا مِنَ الْاٰصَارِ وَالْاَجْرَامِ\nALLAAHUMMA SAHHIL LANAA FEEHI MAA QASAMTAHOO MIN RIZQIKA WA YASSIR MAA QADDARTAHOO MIN AMRIKA WAJ'ALHU HALAALAN TAYYIBAN NAQIYYAN MINAL AATHAAMI KHAALISAN MINAL AASAARI WAL AJRAAM\nO Allah, (please do) make easy for us the gaining of Your sustenance that You decide for us, facilitate for us gaining that which You decide for us, and make it pure, empty of sins, and free from offenses and flaws.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ لَا تُطْعِمْنَا اِلَّا طَيِّبًا غَيْرَ خَبِيْثٍ وَلَا حَرَامٍ، وَاجْعَلْ رِزْقَكَ لَنَا حَلَالًا لَا يَشُوْبُهٗ دَنَسٌ وَلَا اَسْقَامٌ\nALLAAHUMMA LAA TUT'IMNAA ILLAA TAYYIBAN GHAYRA KHABEETHIN WA LAA HARAAMIN WAJ'AL RIZQAKA LANAA HALAALAN LAA YASHOOBUHOO DANASUN WA LAA ASQAAM\nO Allah, (please) do not feed us except the good that is neither bad nor forbidden. (Please do) let the sustenance that You decide for us be legal, carrying neither filth nor diseases.\nيَا مَنْ عِلْمُهٗ بِالسِّرِّ كَعِلْمِهٖ بِالْاِعْلَانِ، يَا مُتَفَضِّلًا عَلٰى عِبادِهٖ بِالْاِحْسَانِ\nYAA MAN I'LMUHOO BIS SIRRI KA'ILMIHEE BIL I'LAANI YAA MUTAFADDILAN A'LAA I'BAADIHEE BIL IHSAAN\nO He Who knows the secret in the same way as He knows the public! O He Who confers upon His servants with benevolence!\nيَا مَنْ هُوَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ وَبِكُلِّ شَيْءٍ عَلِيْمٌ خَبِيْرٌ\nYAA MAN HUWA A'LAA KULLI SHAY'IN QADEERUN WA BIKULLI SHAY'IN A'LEEMUN KHABEER\nO He Who has power over all things and has acquaintance with all things!\nاَلْهِمْنَا ذِكْرَكَ وَجَنِّبْنَا عُسْرَكَ، وَاَنِلْنَا يُسْرَكَ، وَاهْدِنَا لِلرَّشَادِ، وَوَفِّقْنَا لِلسَّدَادِ\nALHIMNAA DHIKRAKA WA JANNIBNAA U'SRAKA WA ANILNAA YUSRAKA WAHDINAA LIR RASHAADI WA WAFFIQNAA LIS SADAAD\n(Please do) bestow upon us with (ceaseless) reference to You, keep us away Your difficulty, make us obtain Your ease, guide us to the right path, lead us to righteousness\nوَاعْصِمْنَا مِنَ الْبَلَايَا، وَصُنَّا مِنَ الْاَوْزَارِ وَالْخَطَايَا\nWA'SIMNAA MINAL BALAAYAA WA SUNNAA MINAL AWZAARI WAL KHATAAYAA\nprotect us against misfortunes, and safeguard us against sins and faults.\nيَا مَنْ لَا يَغْفِرُ عَظِيْمَ الذُّنُوْبِ غَيْرُهٗ، وَلَا يَكْشِفُ السُّوٓءَ اِلَّا هُوَ\nYAA MAN LAA YAGHFIRU A'ZEEMADH DHUNOOBI GHAYRUHOO WA LAA YAKSHIFUS SOO'A ILLAA HUW\nO He save Whom none forgives the grave sins and none can relieve from hardships!\nيَا اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ، وَاَكْرَمَ الْاَكْرَمِيْنَ\nYAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEENA WA AKRAMAL AKRAMEEN\nO most Merciful of all those who show mercy and most Generous of all those who show generosity!\nصَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاَهْلِ بَيْتِهِ الطَّيِّبِيْنَ، وَاجْعَلْ صِيَامَنَا مَقْبُوْلًا، وَبِالْبِرِّ وَالتَّقْوٰى مَوْصُوْلًا\nSALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AHLI BAYTIHIT TAYYIBEENA WAJ'AL SIYAAMANAA MAQBOOLAN WA BIL BIRRI WAT TAQWAA MAWSOOLAA\n(Please do) send blessings to Muhammad and his Household the pure and decide our fasting to be acceptable and connected to piety and godliness.\nوَكَذٰلِكَ فَاجْعَلْ سَعْيَنَا مَشْكُوْرًا وَقِيَامَنَا مَبْرُوْرًا، وَقُرْاٰنَنَا مَرْفُوْعًا، وَدُعَاۤءَنَا مَسْمُوْعًا\nWA KADHAALIKA FAJ'AL SA'YANAA MASHKOORAN WA QIYAAMANAA MABROORAN WA QUR'AANANAA MARFOO'AN WA DU'AA'ANAA MASMOO'AA\nSimilarly, (please do) decide our efforts to be praiseworthy, our acts of worship admissible, our reciting of the Qur'an raised (to the heavens), and our supplications responded.\nوَاهْدِنَا لِلْحُسْنٰى، وَجَنِّبْنَا الْعُسْرٰى، وَيَسِّرْنَا لِلْيُسْرٰى، وَاَعْلِ لَنَا الدَّرَجَاتِ، وَضَاعِفْ لَنَا الْحَسَنَاتِ\nWAHDINAA LIL HUSNAA WA JANNIBNAL U'SRAA WA YASSIRNAA LIL YUSRAA WA A'LI LANAD DARAJAATI WA DAA'IF LANAL HASANAAT\n(Please do) guide us to the most excellent way, save us from difficulties, facilitate for us the easy end, elevate our ranks, double the rewards for our good deeds\nوَاقْبَلْ مِنَّا الصَّوْمَ وَالصَّلَاةَ، وَاسْمَعْ مِنَّا الدَّعَوَاتِ، وَاغْفِرْ لَنَا الْخَطِيْئَاتِ، وَتَجَاوَزْ عَنَّا السَّيِّئَاتِ\nWAQBAL MINNAS SAWMA WAS SALAATA WASMA' MINNAD DA'AWAATI WAGHFIR LANAL KHATEE'AATI WA TAJAAWAZ A'NNAS SAYYI'AAT\naccept our fasting and prayers, react to our supplications, forgive our sins, overlook our wrongdoings\nوَاجْعَلْنَا مِنَ الْعَامِلِيْنَ الْفَاۤئِزِيْنَ، وَلَا تَجْعَلْنَا مِنَ الْمَغْضُوْبِ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلَا الضَّآلِّيْنَ\nWAJ'ALNAA MINAL A'AMILEENAL FAA'IZEENA WA LAA TAJ'ALNAA MINAL MAGHDOOBI A'LAYHIM WA LAD DAALLEEN\nmake us of the successful worshippers, and do not include us with those who earn Your anger nor of those who go astray\nحَتّٰى يَنْقَضِيَ شَهْرُ رَمَضَانَ عَنَّا وَقَدْ قَبِلْتَ فِيْهِ صِيَامَنَا وَقِيَامَنَا، وَزَكَّيْتَ فِيْهِ اَعْمَالَنَا، وَغَفَرْتَ فِيْهِ ذُنُوْبَنَا، وَاَجْزَلْتَ فِيْهِ مِنْ كُلِّ خَيْرٍ نَصِيْبَنَا\nHATTAA YANQADIYA SHAHRU RAMADAANA A'NNAA WA QAD QABILTA FEEHI SIYAAMANAA WA QIYAAMANAA WA ZAKKAYTA FEEHI A'MAALANAA WA GHAFARTA FEEHI DHUNOOBANAA WA AJZALTA FEEHI MIN KULLI KHAYRIN NASEEBANAA\nso that when the month of Ramadan elapses, You shall have accepted our fasting and acts of worship, blessed our deeds, forgiven our sins, and doubled our shares from all good things.\nفَاِنَّكَ الْاِلٰهُ الْمُجِيْبُ، وَالرَّبُّ الْقَرِيْبُ، وَاَنْتَ بِكُلِّ شَيْءٍ مُحِيْطٌ\nFA-INNAKAL ILAAHUL MUJEEBU WAR RABBUL QAREEBU WA ANTA BIKULLI SHAY'IN MUHEET\nVerily, You are the God Who responds, the Lord Who is Nigh, and You encompass all things.",
    "Allahumma Rabba Shahri Ramadan\nاَللّٰهُمَّ رَبَّ شَهْرِ رَمَضَانَ، مُنَزِّلَ الْقُرْاٰنِ\nALLAAHUMMA RABBA SHAHRI RAMADAANA MUNAZZILAL QUR'AAN\nO Allah, the Lord of the month of Ramadan and the Revealer of the Qur'an.\nهٰذَا شَهْرُ رَمَضَانَ الَّذِيْ اَنْزَلْتَ فِيْهِ الْقُرْاٰنَ، وَاَنْزَلْتَ فِيْهِ اٰيَاتٍ بَيِّنَاتٍ مِنَ الْهُدٰى وَالْفُرْقَانِ\nHAADHAA SHAHRU RAMADAANAL LADHEE ANZALTA FEEHIL QUR'AANA WA ANZALTA FEEHI AAYAATIN BAYYINAATIN MINAL HUDAA WAL FURQAAN\nThis is the month of Ramadan in which You revealed the Qur'an and revealed therein chapters of true guidance and distinction (between the right and the wrong).\nاَللّٰهُمَّ ارْزُقْنَا صِيَامَهٗ، وَاَعِنَّا عَلٰى قِيَامِهٖ\nALLAAHUMMAR ZUQNAA SIYAAMAHOO WA A'INNAA A'LAA QIYAAMIH\nO Allah, make us observe fast in its days and remain awake in its nights to pray.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ سَلِّمْهُ لَنَا وَسَلِّمْنَا فِيْهِ وَتَسَلَّمْهُ مِنَّا فِيْ يُسْرٍ مِنْكَ وَمُعَافَاةٍ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLIMHU LANAA WA SALLIMNAA FEEHI WA TASALLAMHU MINNAA FEE YUSRIN MINKA WA MU'AAFAAH\nO Allah, let it be peaceful for us, keep us in sound condition for it, and receive it from us with easiness and wellbeing.\nوَاجْعَلْ فِيْمَا تَقْضِيْ وَتُقَدِّرُ مِنَ الْاَمْرِ الْمَحْتُوْمِ وَفِيْمَا تَفْرُقُ مِنَ الْاَمْرِ الْحَكِيْمِ فِيْ لَيْلَةِ الْقَدْرِ مِنَ الْقَضَاۤءِ الَّذِيْ لَا يُرَدُّ وَلَا يُبَدَّلُ\nWAJ'AL FEEMAA TAQDEE WA TUQADDIRU MINAL AMRIL MAHTOOMI WA FEEMAA TAFRUQU MINAL AMRIL HAKEEMI FEE LAYLATIL QADRI MINAL QADAA'IL LADHEE LAA YURADDU WA LAA YUBADDAL\nWhile taking decisions from among Your inevitable decisions and from among that which You decide from the wise affairs at the Destiny Night from the act that is neither rejected nor altered\nاَنْ تَكْتُبَنِيْ مِنْ حُجَّاجِ بَيْتِكَ الْحَرَامِ الْمَبْرُوْرِ حَجُّهُمُ، الْمَشْكُوْرِ سَعْيُهُمُ، الْمَغْفُوْرِ ذُنُوْبُهُمُ، الْمُكَفَّرِ عَنْهُمْ سَيِّئَاتُهُمْ\nAN TAKTUBANEE MIN HUJJAAJI BAYTIKAL HARAAMIL MABROORI HAJJUHUMUL MASHKOORI SA'YUHUMUL MAGHFOORI DHUNOOBUHUMUL MUKAFFARI A'NHUM SAYYI'AATUHUM\n(please) write my name in the list of those pilgrims to Your Sacred House whose pilgrimage receives Your approval, whose efforts are appreciated, whose sins are forgiven, and whose wrongdoings are overlooked.\nوَاجْعَلْ فِيْمَا تَقْضِيْ وَتُقَدِّرُ اَنْ تُطِيْلَ عُمْرِيْ وَتُوَسِّعَ عَلَيَّ مِنَ الرِّزْقِ الْحَلَالِ\nWAJ'AL FEEMAA TAQDEE WA TUQADDIRU AN TUTEELA U'MREE WA TUWASSI'A A'LAYYA MINAR RIZQIL HALAAL\nWhile making decisions and rendering possible things and events, (please) grant me long lifetime and expand my sustenance, making it from legal sources only.",
    "Sahifa Dua 44: Welcoming Ramazan\nالْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ الَّذِي هَدَانَا لِحَمْدِهٖ\nAL-HAMDU LILLAAHIL LADHEE HADAANAA LIHAMDIH\nPraise belongs to God who guided us to His praise\nوَجَعَلَنَا مِنْ اَهْلِهٖ لِنَكُونَ لِاِحْسَانِهٖ مِنَ الشَّاكِرِينَ\nWA JA'ALANAA MIN AHLIHEE LINAKOONA LI-IHSAANIHEE MINASH SHAAKIREEN\nand placed us among the people of praise, that we might be among the thankful for His beneficence\nوَلِيَجْزِيَنَا عَلَى ذَلِكَ جَزَاءَ الْمُحْسِنِينَ\nWA LIYAJZIYANAA A'LAA DHAALIKA JAZAA'AL MUHSINEEN\nand that He might recompense us for that with the recompense of the good-doers!\nوَالْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ الَّذِي حَبَانَا بِدِينِهٖ\nWAL HAMDU LILLAAHIL LADHEE HABAANAA BIDEENIH\nAnd praise belongs to God who showed favour to us through His religion,\nوَاخْتَصَّنَا بِمِلَّتِهٖ، وَسَبَّلَنَا فِي سُبُلِ اِحْسَانِهٖ\nWAKHTASSANAA BIMILLATIHEE WA SABBALANAA FEE SUBULI IHSAANIH\nsingled us out for His creed, and directed us onto the roads of His beneficence,\nلِنَسْلُكَهَا بِمَنِّهٖ اِلَى رِضْوَانِهٖ\nLINASLUKAHAA BIMANNIHEE ILAA RIDWAANIH\nin order that through His kindness we might travel upon them to His good pleasure,\nحَمْداً يَتَقَبَّلُهٗ مِنَّا، وَيَرْضَى بِهٖ عَنَّا\nHAMDAN YATAQABBALUHOO MINNAA WA YARDAA BIHEE A'NNAA\na praise which He will accept from us and through which He will be pleased with us!\nوَالْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ الَّذِي جَعَلَ مِنْ تِلْكَ السُّبُلِ شَهْرَهٗ شَهْرَ رَمَضَانَ\nWAL HAMDU LILLAAHIL LADHEE JA'ALA MIN TILKAS SUBULI SHAHRAHOO SHAHRA RAMADAAN\nAnd praise belongs to God who appointed among those roads His month, the month of Ramadan,\nشَهْرَ الصِّيَامِ، وَشَهْرَ الْاِسْلَامِ، وَشَهْرَ الطَّهُورِ\nSHAHRAS SIYAAMI WA SHAHRAL ISLAAMI WA SHAHRAT TAHOOR\nthe month of fasting, the month of submission, the month of purity,\nوَشَهْرَ التَّمْحِيصِ، وَشَهْرَ الْقِيَامِ\nWA SHAHRAT TAMHEESI WA SHAHRAL QIYAAM\nthe month of putting to test, the month of standing in prayer,\nالَّذِي اُنْزِلَ فِيهِ الْقُرْاٰنُ، هُدًى لِلنَّاسِ\nALLADHEE UNZILA FEEHIL QUR'AANU HUDAN LIN NAAS\n\"in which the Qur'an was sent down as guidance to the people,\nوَبَيِّنَاتٍ مِنَ الْهُدَى وَالْفُرْقَانِ\nWA BAYYINAATIN MINAL HUDAA WAL FURQAAN\nand as clear signs of the Guidance and the Separator\" (2:185)!\nفَاَبَانَ فَضِيلَتَهٗ عَلَى سَائِرِ الشُّهُورِ\nFA-ABAANA FADEELATAHOO A'LAA SAA'IRISH SHUHOOR\nHe clarified its excellence over other months\nبِمَا جَعَلَ لَهٗ مِنَ الْحُرُمَاتِ الْمَوْفُورَةِ، وَالْفَضَائِلِ الْمَشْهُورَةِ\nBIMAA JA'ALA LAHOO MINAL HURUMAATIL MAWFOORATI WAL FADAA'ILIL MASH-HOORAH\nby the many sacred things and well-known excellencies which He placed therein,\nفَحَرَّمَ فِيهِ مَا اَحَلَّ فِي غَيْرِهٖ اِعْظَاماً\nFAHARRAMA FEEHI MAA AHALLA FEE GHAYRIHEE I'ZAAMAA\nfor He made unlawful in it what He declared lawful in others to magnify it,\nوَحَجَرَ فِيهِ الْمَطَاعِمَ وَالْمَشَارِبَ اِكْرَاماً\nWA HAJARA FEEHIL MATAA'IMA WAL MASHAARIBA IKRAAMAA\nHe prohibited foods and drinks in it to honour it,\nوَجَعَلَ لَهٗ وَقْتاً بَيِّناً لَا يُجِيزُ جَلَّ وَعَزَّ اَنْ يُقَدَّمَ قَبْلَهٗ\nWA JA'ALA LAHOO WAQTAN BAYYINAN LAA YUJEEZU JALLA WA A'ZZA AN YUQADDAMA QABLAH\nand He appointed for it a clear time which He (majestic and mighty is He) allows not to be set forward\nوَلَا يَقْبَلُ اَنْ يُؤَخَّرَ عَنْهُ\nWA LAA YAQBALU AN YU'AKHKHARA A'NH\nand accepts not to be placed behind.\nثُمَّ فَضَّلَ لَيْلَةً وَاحِدَةً مِنْ لَيَالِيهِ عَلَى لَيَالِي اَلْفِ شَهْرٍ\nTHUMMA FADDALA LAYLATAN WAAHIDATAN MIN LAYAALEEHI A'LAA LAYAALEE ALFI SHAHR\nThen He made one of its nights surpass the nights of a thousand months\nوَسَمَّاهَا لَيْلَةَ الْقَدْرِ\nWA SAMMAAHAA LAYLATAL QADR\nand named it the Night of Decree;\nتَنَزَّلُ الْمَلَائِكَةُ وَالرُّوحُ فِيهَا بِاِذْنِ رَبِّهِمْ مِنْ كُلِّ اَمْرٍ\nTANAZZALUL MALAA'IKATU WAR ROOHU FEEHAA BI-IDHNI RABBIHIM MIN KULLI AMR\n\"in it the angels and the Spirit descend by the leave of their Lord upon every command,\nسَلَامٌ، دَائِمُ الْبَرَكَةِ اِلَى طُلُوعِ الْفَجْرِ\nSALAAMUN DAA'IMUL BARAKATI ILAA TULOO'IL FAJR\na peace\" (97:4-5) constant in blessings until the rising of the dawn\nعَلَى مَنْ يَشَاءُ مِنْ عِبَادِهٖ بِمَا اَحْكَمَ مِنْ قَضَائِهِ\nA'LAA MAN YASHAA'U MIN I'BAADIHEE BIMAA AHKAMA MIN QADAA'IH\nupon whomsoever He will of His servants according to the decision He has made firm.\nاللَّهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلَى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِهِ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIH\nO God, bless Muhammad and his Household,\nوَاَلْهِمْنَا مَعْرِفَةَ فَضْلِهٖ وَاِجْلَالَ حُرْمَتِهٖ\nWA ALHIMNAA MA'RIFATA FADLIHEE WA IJLAALA HURMATIH\ninspire us with knowledge of its excellence, veneration of its inviolability,\nوَالتَّحَفُّظَ مِمَّا حَظَرْتَ فِيهِ\nWAT TAHAFFUZA MIMMAA HAZARTA FEEH\nand caution against what You have forbidden within it,\nوَاَعِنَّا عَلَى صِيَامِهٖ بِكَفِّ الْجَوَارِحِ عَنْ مَعَاصِيكَ\nWA A'INNAA A'LAA SIYAAMIHEE BIKAFFIL JAWAARIHI A'N MA'AASEEK\nand help us to fast in it by our restraining our limbs from acts of disobedience toward You\nوَاسْتِعْمَالِهَا فِيهِ بِمَا يُرْضِيكَ\nWASTI'MAALIHAA FEEHI BIMAA YURDEEK\nand our employing them in that which pleases You,\nحَتَّى لَا نُصْغِيَ بِاَسْمَاعِنَا اِلَى لَغْوٍ\nHATTAA LAA NUSGHIYA BI-ASMAA'INAA ILAA LAGHW\nso that we lend not our ears to idle talk\nوَلَا نُسْرِعَ بِاَبْصَارِنَا اِلَى لَهْوٍ\nWA LAA NUSRI'A BI-ABSAARINAA ILAA LAHW\nand hurry not with our eyes to diversion,\nوَحَتَّى لَا نَبْسُطَ اَيْدِيَنَا اِلَى مَحْظُورٍ\nWA HATTAA LAA NABSUTA AYDIYANAA ILAA MAHZOOR\nwe stretch not our hands toward the forbidden\nوَلَا نَخْطُوَ بِاَقْدَامِنَا اِلَى مَحْجُورٍ\nWA LAA NAKHTUWA BI-AQDAAMINAA ILAA MAHJOOR\nand stride not with our feet toward the prohibited,\nوَحَتَّى لَا تَعِيَ بُطُونُنَا اِلَّا مَا اَحْلَلْتَ\nWA HATTAA LAA TA'IYA BUTOONUNAA ILLAA MAA AHLALT\nour bellies hold only what You have made lawful\nوَلَا تَنْطِقَ اَلْسِنَتُنَا اِلَّا بِمَا مَثَّلْتَ\nWA LAA TANTIQA ALSINATUNAA ILLAA BIMAA MATHTHALT\nand our tongues speak only what You have exemplified,\nوَلَا نَتَكَلَّفَ اِلَّا مَا يُدْنِي مِنْ ثَوَابِكَ\nWA LAA NATAKALLAFA ILLAA MAA YUDNEE MIN THAWAABIK\nwe undertake nothing but what brings close to Your reward\nوَلَا نَتَعَاطَى اِلَّا الَّذِي يَقِي مِنْ عِقَابِكَ\nWA LAA NATA'AATAA ILLAL LADHEE YAQEE MIN I'QAABIK\nand pursue nothing but what protects from Your punishment!\nثُمَّ خَلِّصْ ذَلِكَ كُلَّهٗ مِنْ رِئَاءِ الْمُرَاءِينَ، وَسُمْعَةِ الْمُسْمِعِينَ\nTHUMMA KHALLIS DHAALIKA KULLAHOO MIN RI'AA'IL MURAA'EENA WA SUM'ATIL MUSMI'EEN\nThen rid all of that from the false show of the false showers and the fame seeking of the fame seekers,\nلَا نُشْرِكُ فِيهِ اَحَداً دُونَكَ\nLAA NUSHRIKU FEEHI AHADAN DOONAK\nlest we associate therein anything with You\nوَلَا نَبْتَغِي فِيهِ مُرَاداً سِوَاكَ\nWA LAA NABTAGHEE FEEHI MURAADAN SIWAAK\nor seek therein any object of desire but You!\nاللَّهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلَى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِهِ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIH\nO God, bless Muhammad and his Household,\nوَقِفْنَا فِيهِ عَلَى مَوَاقِيتِ\nWA QIFNAA FEEHI A'LAA MAWAAQEET\nin it make us attend to the appointed moments\nالصَّلَوَاتِ الْخَمْسِ بِحُدُودِهَا الَّتِي حَدَّدْتَ\nAS-SALAWAATIL KHAMSI BIHUDOODIHAL LATEE HADDADT\nof the five prayers within the bounds You have set,\nوَفُرُوضِهَا الَّتِي فَرَضْتَ، وَوَظَائِفِهَا الَّتِي وَظَّفْتَ\nWA FUROODIHAL LATEE FARADTA WA WAZAA'IFIHAL LATEE WAZZAFT\nthe obligations You have decreed, the duties You have assigned,\nوَاَوْقَاتِهَا الَّتِي وَقَّتَّ\nWA AWQAATIHAL LATEE WAQQATT\nand the times You have specified;\nوَاَنْزِلْنَا فِيهَا مَنْزِلَةَ الْمُصِيبِينَ لِمَنَازِلِهَا\nWA ANZILNAA FEEHAA MANZILATAL MUSEEBEENA LIMANAAZILIHAA\nand in the prayers make us alight in the station of the keepers of their stations,\nالْحَافِظِينَ لِاَرْكَانِهَا، الْمُؤَدِّينَ لَهَا\nAL-HAAFIZEENA LI-ARKAANIHAL MU'ADDEENA LAHAA\nthe guardians of their pillars, their performers in their times,\nفِي اَوْقَاتِهَا عَلَى مَا سَنَّهٗ عَبْدُكَ وَرَسُولُكَ صَلَوَاتُكَ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهِ\nFEE AWQAATIHAA A'LAA MAA SANNAHOO A'BDUKA WA RASOOLUKA SALAWAATUKA A'LAYHI WA AALIH\nas Your servant and Your messenger set down in his Sunna (Your blessings be upon him and his Household)\nفِي رُكُوعِهَا وَسُجُودِهَا وَجَمِيعِ فَوَاضِلِهَا\nFEE RUKOO'IHAA WA SUJOODIHAA WA JAMEE'I FAWAADILIHAA\nin their bowings, their prostrations, and all their excellent acts,\nعَلَى اَتَمِّ الطَّهُورِ وَاَسْبَغِهٖ، وَاَبْيَنِ الْخُشُوعِ وَاَبْلَغِهٖ\nA'LAA ATAMMIT TAHOORI WA ASBAGHIHEE WA ABYANIL KHUSHOO'I WA ABLAGHIH\nwith the most complete and ample ritual purity and the most evident and intense humility!\nوَوَفِّقْنَا فِيهِ لِاَنْ نَصِلَ اَرْحَامَنَا بِالْبِرِّ وَالصِّلَةِ\nWA WAFFIQNAA FEEHI LI-AN NASILA ARHAAMANAA BIL BIRRI WAS SILAH\nGive us success in this month to tighten our bonds of kin with devotion and gifts,\nوَاَنْ نَتَعَاهَدَ جِيرَانَنَا بِالْاِفْضَالِ وَالْعَطِيَّةِ\nWA AN NATA'AAHADA JEERAANANAA BIL IFDAALI WAL A'TIYYAH\nattend to our neighbours with bestowal and giving,\nوَاَنْ نُخَلِّصَ اَمْوَالَنَا مِنَ التَّبِعَاتِ\nWA AN NUKHALLISA AMWAALANAA MINAT TABI'AAT\nrid our possessions from claims,\nوَاَنْ نُطَهِّرَهَا بِاِخْرَاجِ الزَّكَوَاتِ\nWA AN NUTAHHIRAHAA BI-IKHRAAJIZ ZAKAWAAT\npurify them through paying the alms,\nوَاَنْ نُرَاجِعَ مَنْ هَاجَرَنَا\nWA AN NURAAJI'A MAN HAAJARANAA\ngo back to him who has gone far from us,\nوَاَنْ نُنْصِفَ مَنْ ظَلَمَنَا\nWA AN NUNSIFA MAN ZALAMANAA\ntreat justly him who has wronged us,\nوَاَنْ نُسَالِمَ مَنْ عَادَانَا\nWA AN NUSAALIMA MAN A'ADAANAA\nmake peace with him who shows enmity toward us\nحَاشَى مَنْ عُودِيَ فِيكَ وَلَكَ\nHAASHAA MAN U'OODIYA FEEKA WA LAK\n(except him who is regarded as an enemy in You and for You,\nفَاِنَّهُ الْعَدُوُّ الَّذِي لَا نُوَالِيهِ\nFA-INNAHUL A'DUWWUL LADHEE LAA NUWAALEEH\nfor he is the enemy whom we will not befriend,\nوَالْحِزْبُ الَّذِي لَا نُصَافِيهِ\nWAL HIZBUL LADHEE LAA NUSAAFEEH\nthe party whom we will not hold dear),\nوَاَنْ نَتَقَرَّبَ اِلَيْكَ فِيهِ مِنَ الْاَعْمَالِ الزَّاكِيَةِ بِمَا تُطَهِّرُنَا بِهٖ مِنَ الذُّنُوبِ\nWA AN NATAQARRABA ILAYKA FEEHI MINAL A'MAALIZ ZAAKIYATI BIMAA TUTAHHIRUNAA BIHEE MINADH DHUNOOB\nand seek nearness to You through blameless works which will purify us from sins\nوَتَعْصِمُنَا فِيهِ مِمَّا نَسْتَاْنِفُ مِنَ الْعُيُوبِ\nWA TA'SIMUNAA FEEHI MIMMAA NASTA'NIFU MINAL U'YOOB\nand preserve us from renewing faults,\nحَتَّى لَا يُورِدَ عَلَيْكَ اَحَدٌ مِنْ مَلَائِكَتِكَ\nHATTAA LAA YOORIDA A'LAYKA AHADUN MIN MALAA'IKATIK\nso that none of Your angels will bring for You\nاِلَّا دُونَ مَا نُورِدُ مِنْ اَبْوَابِ الطَّاعَةِ لَكَ، وَاَنْوَاعِ الْقُرْبَةِ اِلَيْكَ\nILLAA DOONA MAA NOORIDU MIN ABWAABIT TAA'ATI LAKA WA ANWAA'IL QURBATI ILAYK\nthe kinds of obedience and sorts of nearness-seeking unless they be less than what we bring!\nاللَّهُمَّ اِنِّي اَسْاَلُكَ بِحَقِّ هَذَا الشَّهْرِ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS'ALUKA BIHAQQI HAADHASH SHAHR\nO God, I ask You by the right of this month\nوَبِحَقِّ مَنْ تَعَبَّدَ لَكَ فِيهِ\nWA BIHAQQI MAN TA'ABBADA LAKA FEEH\nand by the right of him who worships You within it\nمِنِ ابْتِدَائِهٖ اِلَى وَقْتِ فَنَائِهٖ\nMINIB TIDAA'IHEE ILAA WAQTI FANAA'IH\nfrom its beginning to the time of its passing,\nمِنْ مَلَكٍ قَرَّبْتَهٗ، اَوْ نَبِيٍّ اَرْسَلْتَهٗ\nMIN MALAKIN QARRABTAHOO AW NABIYYIN ARSALTAH\nwhether angel You have brought nigh to You, prophet You have sent,\nاَوْ عَبْدٍ صَالِحٍ اخْتَصَصْتَهٗ\nAW A'BDIN SAALIHINIKH TASASTAH\nor righteous servant You have singled out,\nاَنْ تُصَلِّيَ عَلَى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِهِ\nAN TUSALLIYA A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIH\nthat You bless Muhammad and his Household,\nوَاَهِّلْنَا فِيهِ لِمَا وَعَدْتَ اَوْلِيَاءَكَ مِنْ كَرَامَتِكَ\nWA AHHILNAA FEEHI LIMAA WA'ADTA AWLIYAA'AKA MIN KARAAMATIK\nmake us worthy of the generosity You have promised Your friends,\nوَاَوْجِبْ لَنَا فِيهِ مَا اَوْجَبْتَ لِاَهْلِ الْمُبَالَغَةِ فِي طَاعَتِكَ\nWA AWJIB LANAA FEEHI MAA AWJABTA LI-AHLIL MUBAALAGHATI FEE TAA'ATIK\nmake incumbent for us what You have made incumbent for those who go to great lengths in obeying You,\nوَاجْعَلْنَا فِي نَظْمِ مَنِ اسْتَحَقَّ الرَّفِيعَ الْاَعْلَى بِرَحْمَتِكَ\nWAJ'ALNAA FEE NAZMI MANIS TAHAQQAR RAFEE'AL A'LAA BIRAHMATIK\nand place us in the ranks of those who deserve through Your mercy the highest elevation!\nاللَّهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلَى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِهِ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIH\nO God, bless Muhammad and his Household,\nوَجَنِّبْنَا الْاِلْحَادَ فِي تَوْحِيدِكَ، وَالْتَّقْصِيرَ فِي تَمْجِيدِكَ\nWA JANNIBNAL ILHAADA FEE TAWHEEDIKA WAT TAQSEERA FEE TAMJEEDIK\nturn us aside from deviation in professing Your Unity, falling short in magnifying You,\nوَالشَّكَّ فِي دِينِكَ، وَالْعَمَى عَنْ سَبِيلِكَ، وَالْاِغْفَالَ لِحُرْمَتِكَ\nWASH SHAKKA FEE DEENIKA WAL A'MAA A'N SABEELIKA WAL IGHFAALA LIHURMATIK\nuncertainty in Your religion, blindness toward Your path, heedlessness of Your inviolability,\nوَالِانْخِدَاعَ لِعَدُوِّكَ الشَّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيمِ\nWAL INKHIDAA'A LI-A'DUWWIKASH SHAYTAANIR RAJEEM\nand being deceived by Your enemy, the accursed Satan!\nاللَّهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلَى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِهِ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIH\nO God, bless Muhammad and his Household,\nوَاِذَا كَانَ لَكَ فِي كُلِّ لَيْلَةٍ مِنْ لَيَالِي شَهْرِنَا هَذَا\nWA IDHAA KAANA LAKA FEE KULLI LAYLATIN MIN LAYAALEE SHAHRINAA HAADHAA\nand when in every night of this month's nights\nرِقَابٌ يُعْتِقُهَا عَفْوُكَ، اَوْ يَهَبُهَا صَفْحُكَ\nRIQAABUN YU'TIQUHAA A'FWUKA AW YAHABUHAA SAFHUK\nYou have necks which Your pardon will release and Your forgiveness disregard,\nفَاجْعَلْ رِقَابَنَا مِنْ تِلْكَ الرِّقَابِ\nFAJ'AL RIQAABANAA MIN TILKAR RIQAAB\nplace our necks among those necks\nوَاجْعَلْنَا لِشَهْرِنَا مِنْ خَيْرِ اَهْلٍ وَاَصْحَابٍ\nWAJ'ALNAA LISHAHRINAA MIN KHAYRI AHLIN WA AS-HAAB\nand place us among the best folk and companions of this our month!\nاللَّهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلَى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِهِ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIH\nO God, bless Muhammad and his Household,\nوَامْحَقْ ذُنُوبَنَا مَعَ امِّحَاقِ هِلَالِهِ\nWAMHAQ DHUNOOBANAA MA'AM MIHAAQI HILAALIH\nefface our sins along with the effacing of its crescent moon,\nوَاسْلَخْ عَنَّا تَبِعَاتِنَا مَعَ انْسِلَاخِ اَيَّامِهٖ\nWASLAKH A'NNAA TABI'AATINAA MA'AN SILAAKHI AYYAAMIH\nand make us pass forth from the ill effects of our acts with the passing of its days,\nحَتَّى يَنْقَضِيَ عَنَّا وَقَدْ صَفَّيْتَنَا فِيهِ مِنَ الْخَطِيئَاتِ\nHATTAA YANQADIYA A'NNAA WA QAD SAFFAYTANAA FEEHI MINAL KHATEE'AAT\nuntil it leaves us behind, while within it You have purified us of offenses\nوَاَخْلَصْتَنَا فِيهِ مِنَ السَّيِّئَاتِ\nWA AKHLASTANAA FEEHI MINAS SAYYI'AAT\nand rid us of evil deeds!\nاللَّهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلَى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِهِ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIH\nO God, bless Muhammad and his Household,\nوَاِنْ مِلْنَا فِيهِ فَعَدِّلْنَا، وَاِنْ زُغْنَا فِيهِ فَقَوِّمْنَا\nWA IN MILNAA FEEHI FA'ADDILNAA WA IN ZUGHNAA FEEHI FAQAWWIMNAA\nand should we go off to one side in this month, set us aright; should we swerve, point us straight;\nوَاِنِ اشْتَمَلَ عَلَيْنَا عَدُوُّكَ الشَّيْطَانُ فَاسْتَنْقِذْنَا مِنْهُ\nWA INISH TAMALA A'LAYNAA A'DUWWUKASH SHAYTAANU FASTANQIDHNAA MINH\nand should Your enemy Satan enwrap us, rescue us from him!\nاللَّهُمَّ اشْحَنْهُ بِعِبَادَتِنَا اِيَّاكَ\nALLAAHUMMASH-HANHU BI-I'BAADATINAA IYYAAK\nO God, fill this month with our worship of You,\nوَزَيِّنْ اَوْقَاتَهٗ بِطَاعَتِنَا لَكَ\nWA ZAYYIN AWQAATAHOO BITAA'ATINAA LAK\nadorn its times with our obedience toward You,\nوَاَعِنَّا فِي نَهَارِهٖ عَلَى صِيَامِهٖ\nWA A'INNAA FEE NAHAARIHEE A'LAA SIYAAMIH\nhelp us during its daytime with its fast,\nوَفِي لَيْلِهٖ عَلَى الصَّلَاةِ\nWA FEE LAYLIHEE A'LAS SALAAH\nand in its night with prayer\nوَالتَّضَرُّعِ اِلَيْكَ، وَالْخُشُوعِ لَكَ\nWAT TADARRU'I ILAYKA WAL KHUSHOO'I LAK\nand pleading toward You, humility toward You,\nوَالذِّلَّةِ بَيْنَ يَدَيْكَ\nWADH DHILLATI BAYNA YADAYK\nand lowliness before You,\nحَتَّى لَا يَشْهَدَ نَهَارُهٗ عَلَيْنَا بِغَفْلَةٍ، وَلَا لَيْلُهٗ بِتَفْرِيطٍ\nHATTAA LAA YASH-HADA NAHAARUHOO A'LAYNAA BIGHAFLATIN WA LAA LAYLUHOO BITAFREET\nso that its daytime may not bear witness against our heedlessness, nor its night against our neglect!\nاللَّهُمَّ وَاجْعَلْنَا فِي سَائِرِ الشُّهُورِ وَالْاَيَّامِ كَذَلِكَ مَا عَمَّرْتَنَا\nALLAAHUMMA WAJ'ALNAA FEE SAA'IRISH SHUHOORI WAL AYYAAMI KADHAALIKA MAA A'MMARTANAA\nO God, make us like this in the other months and days as long as You give us life,\nوَاجْعَلْنَا مِنْ عِبَادِكَ الصَّالِحِينَ\nWAJ'ALNAA MIN I'BAADIKAS SAALIHEEN\nand place us among Your righteous servants,\nالَّذِينَ يَرِثُونَ الْفِرْدَوْسَ هُمْ فِيهَا خَالِدُونَ\nALLADHEENA YARITHOONAL FIRDAWSA HUM FEEHAA KHAALIDOON\n\"those who shall inherit Paradise, therein dwelling forever\" (23:11),\nوَالَّذِينَ يُؤْتُونَ مَا اٰتَوْا وَقُلُوبُهُمْ\nWAL LADHEENA YU'TOONA MAA AATAW WA QULOOBUHUM\n\"those who give what they give, while their hearts quake,\nوَجِلَةٌ، اَنَّهُمْ اِلَى رَبِّهِمْ رَاجِعُونَ\nWAJILATUN ANNAHUM ILAA RABBIHIM RAAJI'OON\nthat they are returning to their Lord\" (23:60),\nوَمِنَ الَّذِينَ يُسَارِعُونَ فِي الْخَيْرَاتِ وَهُمْ لَهَا سَابِقُونَ\nWA MINAL LADHEENA YUSAARI'OONA FIL KHAYRAATI WA HUM LAHAA SAABIQOON\nthose who \"..vie in good works, outracing to them\" (23:61)!\nاللَّهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلَى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِهِ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIH\nO God, bless Muhammad and his Household\nفِي كُلِّ وَقْتٍ وَكُلِّ اَوَانٍ وَعَلَى كُلِّ حَالٍ\nFEE KULLI WAQTIN WA KULLI AWAANIN WA A'LAA KULLI HAAL\nin every time, in all moments, and in every state,\nعَدَدَ مَا صَلَّيْتَ عَلَى مَنْ صَلَّيْتَ عَلَيْهِ\nA'DADA MAA SALLAYTA A'LAA MAN SALLAYTA A'LAYH\nto the number that You have blessed whomsoever You have blessed\nوَاَضْعَافَ ذَلِكَ كُلِّهٖ بِالْاَضْعَافِ\nWA AD'AAFA DHAALIKA KULLIHEE BIL AD'AAF\nand to multiples of all that, through multiples\nالَّتِي لَا يُحْصِيهَا غَيْرُكَ\nALLATEE LAA YUHSEEHAA GHAYRUK\nwhich none can count but You!\nاِنَّكَ فَعَّالٌ لِمَا تُرِيدُ\nINNAKA FA''AALUN LIMAA TUREED\nSurely You are Accomplisher of what You desire.",
    "Allahumma Inna Hadha Shahru Ramadan\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنَّ هٰذَا شَهْرُ رَمَضَانَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNA HAADHAA SHAHRU RAMADAAN\nO Allah: This month of Ramadhan,\nاَلَّذي اَنْزَلْتَ فِيْهِ الْقُرْاٰنَ\nALLADHEE ANZALTA FEEHIL QUR'AAN\nin which You revealed the Qur'an,\nهُدىً لِلنّاسِ وَبَيِّناتٍ مِنَ الْهُدى وَالْفُرْقَانِ\nHUDAA LIN NAASI WA BAYYINAATIN MINAL HUDAA WAL FURQAAN\nAs guidance for people and clear proofs of true guidance and distinction (between the right and the wrong),\nقَدْ حَضَرَ\nQAD HADAR\nHas commenced.\nيا رَبِّ اَعوذُ بِكَ فِيْهِ مِنَ الشَّيْطانِ الرَّجيمِ\nYAA RABBI A'OODHU BIKA FEEHI MINASH SHAYTAANIR RAJEEM\nO Allah: in this month, I seek Your protection against Satan, the accursed,\nوَمِنْ مَكْرِهٖ وَحِيَلِهٖ\nWA MIN MAKRIHEE WA HIYALIH\nAnd against his tricks and his ruses,\nوَخِداعِهٖ وَحَبائِلِهٖ\nWA KHIDAA'IHEE WA HABAA'ILIH\nAnd his deception and his trickeries,\nوَجُنودِهٖ وَخَيلِهٖ\nWA JUNOODIHEE WA KHAYLIH\nAnd his parties and his riding forces,\nوَرِجْلِهٖ وَوَساوِسِهٖ\nWA RIJLIHEE WA WASAAWISIH\nAnd his on foot forces and his evil inspirations,\nوَمِنَ الضَّلالِ بَعْدَ الْهُدى\nWA MINAD DALAALI BA'DAL HUDAA\nAnd against straying off after being guided,\nوَمِنَ الكُفْرِ بَعْدَ الاِيمانِ\nWA MINAL KUFRI BA'DAL EEMAAN\nAnd against atheism after belief,\nوَمِنَ النِّفاقِ وَالرِّياءِ وَالجِناياتِ\nWA MINAN NIFAAQI WAR RIYAA'I WAL JINAAYAAT\nAnd against hypocrisy and showing off and felonies,\nوَمِنْ شَرِّ الوِسْواسِ الخَنّاسِ\nWA MIN SHARRIL WISWAASIL KHANNAAS\nAnd against the evil of the whisperings of the slinking Devil,\nالَّذي يُوَسْوِسُ فِيْ صُدورِ النّاسِ\nALLADHEE YUWASWISU FEE SUDOORIN NAAS\nWho whispers into the hearts of men;\nمِنَ الجِنَّةِ وَالنّاسِ\nMINAL JINNATI WAN NAAS\nFrom among the jinn and the men.\nاللّهُمَّ وَارْزُقْني صِيامَهٗ وَقِيامَهٗ\nALLAAHUMMA WARZUQNEE SIYAAMAHOO WA QIYAAMAH\nO Allah: and confer upon me with the fasting and the doing of acts of worship during this month,\nوَالعَمَلَ فيهِ بِطاعَتِكَ\nWAL A'MALA FEEHI BITAA'ATIK\nAnd with the doing of acts of obedience to You,\nوَطاعَةِ رَسولِكَ وَاُولي الْاَمْرِ\nWA TAA'ATI RASOOLIKA WA ULIL AMR\nAnd to Your Messenger and the Men in Authority,\nعَلَيهِ وَعَلَيهِمُ السَّلامُ\nA'LAYHI WA A'LAYHIMUS SALAAM\nMay peace be upon him and them,\nوَما قَرَّبَ مِنْكَ\nWA MAA QARRABA MINK\nAnd the doing of whatever act that takes me near You,\nوَجَنِّبْني مَعاصِيكَ\nWA JANNIBNEE MA'AASEEK\nAnd (please) take me away from acts of disobedience to You.\nوَارْزُقْني فيهِ التَّوْبَةَ وَالاِنابَةَ وَالاِجابَةَ\nWARZUQNEE FEEHIT TAWBATA WAL INAABATA WAL IJAABAH\nAnd confer upon me in this month with repentance, turning to You, and responding to Your instructions.\nوَاَعِذْني فيهِ مِنَ الغيبَةِ وَالكَسَلِ وَالفَشَلِ\nWA A'IDHNEE FEEHI MINAL GHEEBATI WAL KASALI WAL FASHAL\nAnd protect me in it against backbiting and lethargy and failure.\nوَاسْتَجِبْ لي فيهِ الدُّعاءَ\nWASTAJIB LEE FEEHID DU'AA'\nAnd respond my prayers in it.\nوَاَصِحَّ لي فيهِ جِسمي وَعَقْلي\nWA ASIHHA LEE FEEHI JISMEE WA A'QLEE\nAnd grant me well-being for my body and my intellect.\nوَفَرِّغْني فيهِ لِطاعَتِكَ وَما قَرَّبَ مِنكَ\nWA FARRIGHNEE FEEHI LITAA'ATIKA WA MAA QARRABA MINK\nAnd grant me time to do acts of obedience to You as well as acts that take me near You.\nيا كَريمُ يا جَوادُ\nYAA KAREEMU YAA JAWAAD\nO the All-generous; O the All-magnanimous.\nيا كَريمُ\nYAA KAREEM\nO the All-generous:\nصَلِّ عَلى مُحَمَّدٍ وَعَلى اَهْلِ بَيْتِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nSALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA A'LAA AHLI BAYTI MUHAMMAD\n(please) send blessings upon Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad,\nعَلَيهِ وَعَلَيهِمُ السَّلامُ\nA'LAYHI WA A'LAYHIMUS SALAAM\nPeace be upon him and them,\nوَكَذالِكَ فَافْعَلْ بِنا\nWA KADHAALIKA FAF'AL BINAA\nAnd do all that to us,\nيا اَرْحَمَ الرّاحِمينَ\nYAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEEN\nO the most Merciful of all those who show mercy.",
    "Duas of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.)\nAt the beginning of Ramazan, recite:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنَّهٗ قَدْ دَخَلَ شَهْرُ رَمَضَانَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNAHOO QAD DAKHALA SHAHRU RAMADAAN\nO Allah, the month of Ramadan has begun.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ رَبَّ شَهْرِ رَمَضَانَ، الَّذِيْ اَنْزَلْتَ فِيْهِ الْقُرْاٰنَ، وَجَعَلْتَهٗ بَيِّنَاتٍ مِنَ الْهُدٰى وَالْفُرْقَانِ\nALLAAHUMMA RABBA SHAHRI RAMADAANAL LADHEE ANZALTA FEEHIL QUR'AANA WA JA'ALTAHOO BAYYINAATIN MINAL HUDAA WAL FURQAAN\nO Allah, the Lord of the month of Ramadan in which You have revealed the Qur'an making it guidance to people and clear proofs of the guidance and the distinction.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ فَبَارِكْ لَنَا فِيْ شَهْرِ رَمَضَانَ، وَاَعِنَّا عَلٰى صِيَامِهٖ وَصَلَوَاتِهٖ وَتَقَبَّلْهُ مِنَّا\nALLAAHUMMA FABAARIK LANAA FEE SHAHRI RAMADAANA WA A'INNAA A'LAA SIYAAMIHEE WA SALAWAATIHEE WA TAQABBALHU MINNAA\nSo, O Allah, please bless us in the month of Ramadan, help us observe fasting and offer prayers in it, and accept from us.\nOn the first night of Ramazan, recite:\nاَلْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِيْ اَكْرَمَنَا بِكَ اَيُّهَا الشَّهْرُ الْمُبَارَكُ\nAL-HAMDU LILLAAHIL LADHEE AKRAMANAA BIKA AYYUHASH SHAHRUL MUBAARAK\nAll praise be to Allah Who has honored us with you, O blessed month.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ فَقَوِّنَا عَلٰى صِيَامِنَا وَقِيَامِنَا، وَثَبِّتْ اَقْدَامَنَا وَانْصُرْنَا عَلَى الْقَوْمِ الْكَافِرِيْنَ\nALLAAHUMMA FAQAWWINAA A'LAA SIYAAMINAA WA QIYAAMINAA WA THABBIT AQDAAMANAA WANSURNAA A'LAL QAWMIL KAAFIREEN\nO Allah, (please do) grant us strength to observe fasting and practice acts of worship in this month, make our steps firm, and assist us against the unbelieving people.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اَنْتَ الْوَاحِدُ فَلَا وَلَدَ لَكَ، وَاَنْتَ الصَّمَدُ فَلَا شِبْهَ لَكَ، وَاَنْتَ الْعَزِيْزُ فَلَا يُعِزُّكَ شَيْءٌ\nALLAAHUMMA ANTAL WAAHIDU FALAA WALADA LAKA WA ANTAS SAMADU FALAA SHIBHA LAKA WA ANTAL A'ZEEZU FALAA YU'IZZUKA SHAY'\nO Allah, You are surely the One; therefore, You have not son. You are the eternally Besought of all; therefore, nothing is like You. You are the Almighty; therefore, nothing can overcome You.\nوَاَنْتَ الْغَنِيُّ وَاَنَا الْفَقِيْرُ، وَاَنْتَ الْمَوْلٰى وَاَنَا الْعَبْدُ\nWA ANTAL GHANIYYU WA ANAL FAQEERU WA ANTAL MAWLAA WA ANAL A'BD\nYou are the Self-sufficient while I am poor. You are the Master while I am (Your) slave.\nوَاَنْتَ الْغَفُوْرُ وَاَنَا الْمُذْنِبُ، وَاَنْتَ الرَّحِيْمُ وَاَنَا الْمُخْطِئُ\nWA ANTAL GHAFOORU WA ANAL MUDHNIBU WA ANTAR RAHEEMU WA ANAL MUKHTI'\nYou are the All-forgiving while I am sinful. You are the All-merciful while I am mistaken.\nوَاَنْتَ الْخَالِقُ وَاَنَا الْمَخْلُوْقُ، وَاَنْتَ الْحَيُّ وَاَنَا الْمَيِّتُ\nWA ANTAL KHAALIQU WA ANAL MAKHLOOQU WA ANTAL HAYYU WA ANAL MAYYIT\nYou are the Creator while I am (Your) creature. You are the Ever-living while I am mortal.\nاَسْاَلُكَ بِرَحْمَتِكَ اَنْ تَغْفِرَ لِيْ وَتَرْحَمَنِيْ، وَتَجَاوَزَ عَنِّي اِنَّكَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ\nAS'ALUKA BIRAHMATIKA AN TAGHFIRA LEE WA TARHAMANEE WA TAJAAWAZA A'NNEE INNAKA A'LAA KULLI SHAY'IN QADEER\nI thus beseech You in the name of Your mercy to forgive me, have mercy upon me, and excuse my offenses. You have power over all things.",
    "Reciting the Quran\nRecite the Holy Quran often in the first hours of Ramazan. Before you begin, recite:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّي اَشْهَدُ اَنَّ هٰذَا كِتَابُكَ الْمُنْزَلُ مِنْ عِنْدِكَ عَلٰى رَسُوْلِكَ مُحَمَّدِ بْنِ عَبْدِاللهِ صَلَّى اللهُ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهِ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE ASH-HADU ANNA HAADHAA KITAABUKAL MUNZALU MIN I'NDIKA A'LAA RASOOLIKA MUHAMMADIBNI A'BDILLAAHI SALLALLAAHU A'LAYHI WA AALIH\nO Allah, I testify that this is the Book revealed by You on Your Messenger Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah, blessings of Allah be on him and on his Household\nوَكَلَامُكَ النَّاطِقُ عَلٰى لِسَانِ نَبِيِّكَ، جَعَلْتَهٗ هَادِيًا مِنْكَ اِلٰى خَلْقِكَ، وَحَبْلًا مُتَّصِلًا فِيْمَا بَيْنَكَ وَبَيْنَ عِبَادِكَ\nWA KALAAMUKAN NAATIQU A'LAA LISAANI NABIYYIKA JA'ALTAHOO HAADIYAN MINKA ILAA KHALQIKA WA HABLAN MUTTASILAN FEEMAA BAYNAKA WA BAYNA I'BAADIK\n(these are) Your Words, Your Prophet gave tongue to, (whom) You appointed as guide for the people, and a connected link between You and Your servants.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّي نَشَرْتُ عَهْدَكَ وَكِتابَكَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE NASHARTU A'HDAKA WA KITAABAK\nO Allah, I am opening Your testament and Your Book.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ فَاجْعَلْ نَظَرِيْ فِيْهِ عِبَادَةً، وَقِرَاۤءَتِي فِيْهِ فِكْرًا، وَفِكْرِيْ فِيْهِ اعْتِبَارًا\nALLAAHUMMA FAJ'AL NAZAREE FEEHI I'BAADATAN WA QIRAA'ATEE FEEHI FIKRAN WA FIKREE FEEHI'TIBAARAA\nO Allah, decide my looking in it to be a kind of worship, my reciting in it to be ponderation, and my ponderation over it to be learning lessons from it.\nوَاجْعَلْنِيْ مِمَّنْ اِتَّعَظَ بِبَيَانِ مَوَاعِظِكَ فِيْهِ، وَاجْتَنَبَ مَعَاصِيْكَ\nWAJ'ALNEE MIMMAN ITTA'AZA BIBAYAANI MAWAA'IZIKA FEEHI WAJTANABA MA'AASEEK\nInclude me with those who take lessons from the elucidation of Your preaches therein and those who accordingly avoid doing acts of disobedience to You.\nوَلَا تَطْبَعْ عِنْدَ قِرَاۤءَتِيْ عَلٰى سَمْعِيْ، وَلَا تَجْعَلْ عَلٰى بَصَرِيْ غِشَاوَةً، وَلَا تَجْعَلْ قِرَاۤءَتِي قِرَاۤءَةً لَا تَدَبُّرَ فِيْهَا\nWA LAA TATBA' I'NDA QIRAA'ATEE A'LAA SAM'EE WA LAA TAJ'AL A'LAA BASAREE GHISHAAWATAN WA LAA TAJ'AL QIRAA'ATEE QIRAA'ATAN LAA TADABBURA FEEHAA\nDo not seal on my hearing while I am reciting it, do not place covering on my sight, and do not decide my reciting to be thoughtless\nبَلِ اجْعَلْنِيْ اَتَدَبَّرُ اٰيَاتِهٖ وَاَحْكَامَهٗ، اٰخِذًا بِشَرَايِعِ دِيْنِكَ\nBALIJ A'LNEE ATADABBARU AAYAATIHEE WA AHKAAMAHOO AAKHIDHAN BISHARAAYI'I DEENIK\nrather, (please) make me ponder over its verses and laws, learning the laws of my religion.\nوَلَا تَجْعَلْ نَظَرِيْ فِيْهِ غَفْلَةً، وَلَا قِرَاۤءَتِيْ هَذَرًا\nWA LAA TAJ'AL NAZAREE FEEHI GHAFLATAN WA LAA QIRAA'ATEE HADHARAA\nDo not decide my looking in it to be inadvertence, and do not allow my reciting to be worthless.\nاِنَّكَ اَنْتَ الرَّؤُوْفُ الرَّحِيْمُ\nINNAKA ANTAR RA'OOFUR RAHEEM\nYou are verily the All-kind, the All-merciful.\nWhen you finish, recite [Dua after Reciting the Holy Quran](A2)."
  ],
  "merits": "Intercourse with one's wife is otherwise discommended on the first night of the Arabic months; this exception is one of the peculiarities of the holy month of Ramadan.\n\nGhusl: A Hadith reads that if one washes himself at the first night of Ramadan, one will be secured against prurigo up to the next Ramadan. Bathing in a flowing river and pouring thirty handfuls of water on the head keeps one mentally pure up to the next Ramadan.\n\nZiyarat: Visiting the holy tomb of Imam al-Husayn (a.s.) on this night brings forgiveness of sins and the like of the reward of those who undertake Hajj and 'Umrah in that year.\n\nAllahumma Inna Hadha al-Shahr al-Mubarak: This supplication is also among the rites of the last night of Sha'ban.\n\nDua Ya Man Yamliku al-Tadbir: Reported in al-Iqbal from Imam Muhammad al-Jawad al-Taqi (a.s.).\n\nAllahumma Rabba Shahri Ramadan: Reported from Imam Ja'far al-Sadiq (a.s.), as mentioned in the book of al-Iqbal.\n\nSahifa Dua 44: The forty-fourth supplication of al-Sahifah al-Kamilah al-Sajjadiyyah, Imam Zayn al-Abidin (a.s.)'s supplication for the coming of the month of Ramadan.\n\nAllahumma Inna Hadha Shahru Ramadan: A lengthy supplication mentioned by Sayyid Ibn Tawus in Iqbal al-A'mal.\n\nDuas of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.): According to a Hadith, the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) used to say the first of these at the beginning of Ramadan, and is also reported to have said the second at the first night of Ramadan.\n\nReciting the Quran: Imam Ja'far al-Sadiq (a.s.) used to say this supplication before he would start reciting the Holy Qur'an, and [Dua after Reciting the Holy Quran](A2) when he finished."
}
